Article 10

(1) The obligations and responsibilities of Customary Institutions in organizing protection for women and children as referred to in Article 6 letter e, include:

a. customary institutions have the responsibility to uphold the dignity and human rights of women and children in accordance with highly valued humanitarian values;
b. responsible for preventing all forms of violence, exploitation, discrimination, mistreatment and/or treatment that degrades the dignity and honor of women and children in the customary environment;
c. ensuring gender equality and children's rights are respected, without discrimination based on gender or age;
d. responsible for raising awareness among customary communities regarding the rights of women and children, including awareness of the importance of protecting and respecting their rights;
e. organizing education and training programs for members of customary communities, especially customary leaders, on the rights of women and children and effective protection methods;
f. providing psychosocial and legal support to victims of violence, exploitation, discrimination, mistreatment and/or treatment that degrades the dignity and honor of women and children including facilitating victims' access to protection and legal institutions;
g. playing an active role in the reporting and law enforcement process regarding cases of violence, exploitation, discrimination, mistreatment and/or treatment that degrades the dignity and honor of women and children in customary communities;
h. facilitating the establishment of PPA institutions at the customary level tasked with protecting their rights and providing assistance and support to victims;
i. integrating customary values that support equality and PPA into community education and outreach programs; and j. building partnerships with non-governmental organizations, protection institutions, and educational institutions to strengthen PPA efforts. (2) The obligations and responsibilities of Business Entities in organizing protection for women and children as referred to in Article 6 letter e, include:
a. obligated to comply with all laws, regulations, and rules related to PPA at national and regional levels; b. providing a safe and supportive work environment, free from harassment, discrimination, violence, mistreatment and/or treatment that degrades the dignity and honor of women and children;
c. providing shelter for female workers at the workplace; d. establishing partnerships with regional governments in PPA; e. providing empowerment to women and children as a shared responsibility with regional government;
f. conducting education programs in communities around the company to raise awareness about PPA;
g. creating PPA policies, programs, and activities;
h. supporting social programs that enhance women's economic independence and support children's education; i. supporting the establishment of protection and service centers for victims of violence against women and children; and
j. supporting PPA programs in Pulang Pisau Regency through Corporate Social Responsibility instruments and/or assistance in other forms in accordance with applicable laws and regulations.

